+/*
+ * drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/gslX680/mtk_gslX680.c
+ *
+ * D17 port of the GSL (Silead) touch-panel driver for the TIMMKOO Q5
+ * (`gsl_tp` @ i2c-0 0x40).  GAP-1 close, bob-m2-spec §1.4.
+ *
+ * Provenance:
+ *  - Driver skeleton: carlitros900/android_kernel_archos_oxygen @ ed79b470,
+ *    drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/gslX68X/mtk_gslX680.c (public
+ *    gslX68X MTK-tpd driver, same silead family as the Q5's; donors pinned in
+ *    manifests/kernel-sources.sha256).  The named priority donors
+ *    (selene/sprout/persimmon/e5fhd) carry no gsl driver at all (selene ships
+ *    only an empty gslX680 Makefile stub); no public source carries the Q5's
+ *    multi-config firmware variant (Sourcegraph global search for
+ *    GSLX680_FW_DSJ / GSLX68X_FW_JX: 0 hits).
+ *  - Q5 firmware + wiring: extracted/decoded from the pinned Lithium blob
+ *    (5217dd41…, decomp d284ba16…, hash-asserted by
+ *    build/extract_gsl_fw_from_blob.py):
+ *      * firmware arrays: gslX680_fw_q5.h (5 configs + GSL_TP_CHECK_FW);
+ *      * panel selection: the blob's gsl_sw_init fingerprint autodetect
+ *        (reg 0xb8 fingerprint scored against 6 known constants, minimum
+ *        score wins, first match in cascade order);
+ *      * I2C "gsl_tp" @ bus 0 addr 0x40 (blob gsl_device_id string + the
+ *        board-info table at VA 0xc0b0af98: "gsl_tp"@0x40, matching the live
+ *        device 0-0040 gsl_tp);
+ *      * reset GPIO14 (GPIO_CTP_RST_PIN), INT GPIO2 pull-up
+ *        (GPIO_CTP_EINT_PIN), EINT channel 2 rising
+ *        (mt_eint_registration(2, EINTF_TRIGGER_RISING, …));
+ *      * power: VIO28@1.8 V + VGP1@2.8 V ("TP" consumer tag).
+ *  - tpd glue: adapted to THIS tree's touch framework
+ *    (drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/mtk_tpd.c): tpd_driver_add()
+ *    registration, tpd_load_status handshake, earlysuspend-based
+ *    suspend/resume — the same way the in-tree ft5336/Goodix9xx drivers
+ *    attach.  (This 3.10.54 tree has no CONFIG_CUSTOM_KERNEL_TOUCHPANEL
+ *    symbol; the driver is selected by CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_MTK_GSL_TP.)
+ *
+ * [BLOB] marks the sites adapted to the Q5's compiled driver behaviour.
+ *
